  "reykjavik.P.list.19.occupation": "Yoga teacher",
  "reykjavik.P.list.2.bio": "Alexandra Briem is a city councillor for Píratar in Reykjavík, born in 1983 and raised in Breiðholt. She has over eight years of experience in the service of the city and has held roles as chair of the city executive board and deputy mayor. She sits on the board of Strætó bs. Alexandra was born in Iceland and says she was raised in Hólahverfi and Seljahverfi, but recently moved downtown, where she now lives in an apartment in a small multi-unit building. She also says that she is trans, a huge nerd, a great idealist in politics, and probably has opinions on everything.\n\nIn recent years Alexandra has worked on the city council, but before that she worked in technical support for a telecom company and in various service-sector jobs, including delivering pizzas, cleaning hotel rooms, and night work caring for patients in a dementia ward. She completed upper secondary school and is about halfway through university studies. Alexandra started showing up with Píratar at the 2013 election watch and formally joined in 2014. She speaks English in addition to Icelandic and says she can also get by a little in Danish and German.\n\nIn her answers, Alexandra says she went into politics because she cannot stand corruption or old-fashioned Icelandic special-interest nonsense and shoddiness. She wants Reykjavík to be excellent, green, and modern, with strong public transport and excellent services, and for the city to be well run and continue to defend human rights and democracy. She mentions Barack Obama first when asked about a political role model, but also says she learned a lot from working with Dagur B. Eggertsson. Alexandra is fond of Freddie Mercury and Queen, and among Icelandic bands she mentions Fræbbblarnir and Stuðmenn. She is especially fond of The Hitchhiker’s Guide to the Galaxy by Douglas Adams and the books of Terry Pratchett, and also mentions books by Iain M. Banks. Among the films she mentions are Groundhog Day and Everything Everywhere All at Once, and she says she also likes anything involving Star Trek or Star Wars. Her main hobby is playing good games with her friends, both board games and role-playing games such as Dungeons and Dragons, but she also enjoys traveling, reading, and politics.",
  "reykjavik.P.list.2.interests.0": "Digital services and technology",
  "reykjavik.P.list.2.interests.1": "Planning and environmental issues",
  "reykjavik.P.list.2.interests.2": "Transport issues",
  "reykjavik.P.list.2.interests.3": "Transparency and democratic participation",
  "reykjavik.P.list.2.occupation": "City Councillor, chair of the city executive committee, deputy mayor",
